            "anno" : "E2F dimerization partner E4orf6/7",
            "comment" : "E4-ORF6/7 is the product of an mRNA spliced from the N-terminus of E4 ORF6 onto ORF7 (PMID 2949089); the HAdV-5 protein is 150 aa and its C-terminal 70 aa form the E2F complex (PMID 1836562); it binds E2F and transactivates the E2 promoter (PMID 1832724), inducing E2F dimerization (PMID 8289811). Literature junction: HAdV-2/HAdV-5 CDS complement(join(..33192,33904..34077)), intron 33193..33903 (PMID 33239457; HAdV-5 numbering from the long-read re-annotation OP218818 of PMID 36095031); verified on AC_000008. No paper gives the junction for other species, so DATABASE-ONLY anchors were also used, each verified on sequence (ATG, GT..AG, clean ORF): HAdV-3 NC_011203, HAdV-12 NC_001460, HAdV-40 NC_001454. Extended to other genomes by pairwise alignment of the donor and acceptor regions to the nearest anchor; where the acceptor region did not align, the unique AG keeping the exon-2 protein in frame; donor rescue likewise. Every distinct product was translated and aligned with the anchors: exon 2 in frame, the conserved C-terminal motif W.[GE]G[GS] present (all four anchors; HAdV-31 reads WEEGS), no ambiguity codes. 471 of 487 references rest on a database-only anchor for the donor or acceptor. MultiFiber: HAdV-F rests on the HAdV-40 database anchor. 136 unique references, products 116-140 aa; min_len = 0.95 x shortest. Replaces the deposit-built references (kept as E4ORF67.fasta.deposit_built), 29/165 of which sat off canonical sites.",
